# Frontend

## Conventions

- React Query keys: `['media']`, `['tags']`, `['tag-groups']`, `['app-settings']`, `['scrape-session']`; invalidate / `setQueryData` after mutations.
- Feedback: `SaveFeedbackProvider` / `notifySaved` / `withSavedFeedback`.
- Confirms: `useConfirm()` — never `window.confirm`.
- Add forms: real `<form onSubmit>` so Enter works.
- Styles: shared classes in `index.css`. Keep `types/appSettings.ts` aligned with backend defaults.
- Settings → Other → Scrape: **Hide Scrape page** stays visible. Everything under it (skip identical, defaults, Scrape browser) renders only while the Scrape page is on. Media detail **Add related files** is a button in the action row; the panel opens under those buttons on the database-id form. **Select a file** opens the shared media grid and hides that form. **Done selecting** hides the grid and shows the id form again. The grid uses `MediaCollectionView` (open file’s tags start selected, **Clear selected**, **Search groups**, **Show hidden tags** from the viewer hide list, six other files per page in one row via `exclude_id`). **Select** marks one or more files to the open one. Typing an id accepts only the local database id.
- `['app-settings']` is seeded in `main.tsx` from `utils/appSettingsCache` (localStorage, written by `AppSettingsSync`) and immediately revalidated — first paint uses real prefs instead of `DEFAULT_APP_SETTINGS`.
- Viewer state derived from settings (`hideExcluded`, `includeDiscarded`, `sort`, `pageSize`) stays `null` until `useApplyAppDefaults` runs: the media query is disabled and controls show no guessed label, so nothing flips after load.
- Viewer `placeholderData` keeps the visible page across tag clicks / paging / sort (filter/sort refetch dims via `media-grid-refreshing` instead of blanking to "Loading..."; page changes stay full opacity) and returns `undefined` only when hide / discarded filters change, so excluded media can never be shown.
- Viewer sidebar: `ViewerTagSidebar` when `viewer_tag_layout` is `sidebar`. Chip mode still uses `TagFilterPanel`. Both build the current-page tag list from non–content-hidden media only (`mediaForPageTagList`). With a tag filter active, list queries also pass locked hide-content tag names as `exclude_tags` (`excludeTagsForMediaQuery`) so blurred files drop out of results until revealed. Tag and group search show a typeahead (`TagSearchSuggest`) with a highlighted match and tag `(count)`.
- Tag-list search: `hooks/useTagSearch` owns search text / match mode / group-filter state and the `matches(tag)` predicate (Tags page, `TagEditor`, `TagListSearch`). `TagListSearch` adds the collapsible **Search tags** toolbar with optional adjacent custom actions, optional **Clear selected**, optional **AND** / **OR** (`onTagModeChange`), and optional separate **Search groups** (`separateGroupSearch`). `TagFilterPanel` turns those extras on for every media grid. Typing in Search tags matches `searchCatalog` (the full library tag list). Enter (when `onSuggestPick` is set) selects the first matching tag, clears the search box, and keeps focus there. On the Scrape page (tag row, Exclude tags, Downloaded previously) the chip cloud stays hidden until Search tags is open and the query is non-empty. Settings **Default exclude tags** and Hidden tags **Individual tags to hide** use Search tags (plus **Add hidden tags** on default exclude) with no chip list (`showChipList={false}` / `searchToolbarOnly`); picks go through the typeahead / Enter. A group filter with an empty tag search stays on the current page’s tags until **Include all tags** on the group panel, which then lists every library tag in the selected groups. When both panels are open, Search groups sits above Search tags. `SearchableTagMultiSelect` / `SingleSelect` keep groups inside Search tags and do not show AND/OR. Esc closes the open panel. Hidden-tag groups use `SearchableGroupMultiSelect`. Media detail `TagEditor`: creating a new tag from search (Enter / Add new tag) passes the selected group filter chips as `group_ids` on `PATCH /media/{id}/tags` so those groups become the new tag’s parents (no selection → default group as before).
- Scrape page: `ScrapePanel` keeps the shared Source/filter form in its own `.panel`, then sibling `ScrapeSourcePanel`s (also `.panel`) for the form's current Source only. Source and Scraper use `ScrapeSelect` (theme menu, not a native `<select>`). Source options are grouped under non-selectable scraper headings (Rule34, Gelbooru, …) and show a short queue line from that source's status panel (`N scraping` while running, plus counts for queue / skipped / errors / cancelled when non-zero). Scraper options show the same line summed across every site that scraper covers. The Scraper list is hidden for Local and otherwise shows every installed scraper. Source and Scraper keep each other in sync: picking a Source switches to a scraper that covers it (keeps the current one when it still fits); picking a Scraper that does not cover the current site switches Source to that scraper's first site. **Unsupported** still shows while incomplete (`processed < total`), running, or holding Queue to scrape. Each owns Run / Stop / Clear queues (`clearScrapeQueues(source)`), a **Clear** on Skipped, Errors, Cancelled, and Queue to scrape (`clearScrapeQueues(source, which)`), and **Retry** on Errors / Skipped (`POST /scrape/retry?source=&which=`). **Skipped** opens nested per-reason sublists (readable labels via `utils/scrapeSkipReasons.ts`), each with its own Retry/Clear (`skip_reason` query on clear/retry). Failed downloads use the Errors queue (not Skipped). Then **Never auto-run scrape** (same `never_auto_run_scrape` as Settings); the status line starts with the panel label. Media detail shows the primary URL always (`url` then inline `primary` to its right; actions Make primary → Edit → Remove in red); extra URLs sit under a collapsed `<details>` spoiler.
- Collapsed chip lists (`CollapsibleTagChipList`, `CollapsibleTagChipSelectList`) render at most `COLLAPSED_CHIP_RENDER_LIMIT` chips until expanded.
- Media cards (`MediaCardThumb`) load `GET /api/media/{id}/preview?size=compact|normal|large&v={file_size}` — a square JPEG — instead of the original file. The browser HTTP-caches that response for about a day (`Cache-Control: max-age=86400`); `v` is the file size so a replaced file does not keep a previous card. Viewer picks the size from the current card width; Downloaded previously and Add related files use compact; duplicate cards use large. `usePreviewPageWindow` still warms the open page first, then `PREVIEW_PAGE_RADIUS` neighbor pages (`frontend/src/utils/previewPageWindow.ts`, default 2) so next/previous pages load (from network or that browser cache). Pages outside the decode window are released from memory; the browser may still serve them from HTTP cache when you return within a day. A video file loads only while that card is playing (hover or autoplay). Detail still uses the full file.
- Device layout prefs (`utils/devicePrefs`, `useDevicePref` / `usePersistedPageSize`): `viewer_page_size`, `tags_page_size`, `scrape_downloads_page_size`, `grid_thumbnail_size`, `viewer_tag_layout`, `viewer_sort`, `viewer_random_seed`, `viewer_filter_tags` (comma-separated), and `viewer_tag_mode` live in `localStorage` (`scrap_device_prefs`) so PC and phone can differ and Viewer sort / tag filter survive leaving the page. First visit may seed from shared settings once.
- Reusable lists: `components/list/PaginationBar` owns paging/count/page-size copy plus a go-to page field (`parseGoToPage`: Enter/blur, clamps to 1…totalPages); `MediaCollectionView` composes tag toolbar + grid + paging with page-specific card/action slots (it keys cards by `item.id`). Select actions share `MediaBulkBar` and `useMediaBulkActions` (Download and Share the selected files across pages, plus discard, delete, tags, and mark). Multi-file Share packs under Chromium’s ~10-file / 50 MiB cap (`packWebShareBatches`). When more than one batch (or any file over 50 MB) is needed, a confirm dialog loops with **Share next** / **Stop** until shareable batches are done (each confirm click is a fresh gesture for `navigator.share`); files over 50 MB are listed and downloaded when the loop finishes or stops. Selection keeps when changing pages; it clears when filters, sort, or page size change. Persist inline page sizes through `usePersistedPageSize` (device-local); pull out-of-range pages back with `usePageClamp`. Settings edits the shared option lists (`viewer_page_sizes` / `tags_page_sizes` via `SettingsPageSizeListEditor` → Edit panel with Save/Cancel); the live selected size stays on each page/device.
- Tag/group DnD: `rowReorder.applyIslandAwareMoveSortOrder` mirrors backend (within-island swap; drop-before island → `start-1` joins; growth pushes the next island via `shiftToClear`).
- After `rowReorder` / Tags / TagGroups order changes: `scripts\run_order_tests.bat` (includes row-reorder and pagination selftests).

## Routes

| Route | Role |
|--------|------|
| `/` | Viewer (filters, grid, detail). **Resolve similar** in the filters row when any identical/similar groups exist (opens `ResolveDuplicatesOverlay`; `DuplicateGroupCard` previews open `MediaDetailModal` scoped to that group’s ids only). **Select** beside Search tags: Shift/drag multi-select, then Download, Share, Discard, Permanent delete, or **Mark as** Identical/Similar (`POST /media/duplicates/mark`, earliest id stays primary; needs two files). Tag toolbar also has **Clear selected** and **Search groups** |
| `/tags`, `/tags/add`, `/tags/groups`, `/tags/settings`, `/tags/groups/settings` | Tags / groups / merge-reset |
| `/scrape` | Scrape (**Source**: Local by default; gallery sites after installing adapters) + **Downloaded previously** (`RecentScrapedMediaPanel`: session by default, optional persisted **Show all downloads** by `scraped_at`; page-size like viewer; × delete; Select + Shift/drag multi-select → Download, Share, Discard, Permanent delete, or **Mark as** Identical/Similar — same bar as the viewer, via `POST /media/bulk` and `POST /media/duplicates/mark`; selection keeps across pages; clears on page size / scope / tag-filter change; detail ‹ › walk the whole session only when no tag filter is active, otherwise the visible page; viewer-style `TagFilterPanel` via `/scrape/recent-media?scope=&tags=` AND filter, including **Clear selected** and **Search groups**) + **Skip identical** (patches `scrape_skip_identical`) + collapsible Similar files (`DuplicatesPanel`: Identical groups can merge — pick keep, union tags/URLs/rating, discard the rest; both kinds have **Keep all** and **Keep selected, discard the rest**, with checkboxes only after Keep selected; 3+ files in one group; collapsed by default) |
| `/duplicates` | → `/scrape` or `/` |
| `/settings` | Theme, Shortcuts (read-only key list), hidden tags, defaults; Other → Tags & duplicates **Resolve similar files** opens the same one-group-at-a-time overlay (`ResolveDuplicatesOverlay` via `ResolveDuplicatesProvider`) |

Nav brand **MediaViewer** → `/`. Esc uses a LIFO stack (`utils/escapeStack`) so the topmost overlay/panel wins (confirm → resolve-duplicates overlay → media modal → expanded tag lists). Detail ←/→, on-screen `<`/`>`, and mouse-wheel tilt left/right use current page `mediaIds` (tilt or ←/→ over a grid switches that grid’s page when detail is closed) (disabled at ends, including in full view). ↑/↓ scroll the media scroller when it overflows (full-view Fill/zoom), otherwise the detail modal panel when that has a vertical scrollbar. Those keys (and rating `1`–`5`) use capture-phase `keydown` via `shouldSkipKeyboardShortcut` so they still work when the detail `<video>` has focus, and so Ctrl/Meta/Alt combos (e.g. Ctrl+F) are not stolen. Media controls (`<`, full-view / `F`, `>`, plus Fit/Fill/± in full view) float bottom-right as an overlay left of Download / rotate / ⋮ so they do not shrink the media stage; Telegram-style chrome also has bottom-left `File N of total` (full filtered list) and those action overlays (`MediaViewerChrome`; ⋮ Share… uses `navigator.share` with a menu-open prefetch for iOS/Android gesture, else download fallback); detail ←/→ loads across pages. The viewer modal is vertically centered in the remaining space (`scrollbar-gutter: stable` so the control panel does not shift). Full view Fit stays contained; Fill (and beyond) pans via an inner scroller while size is measured on an outer padded frame (avoids scrollbar flicker). Scroll wrappers drop max-height/width when an axis overflows so tall Fill images can reach the top. Full view is edge-to-edge (no backdrop/media padding); Fill pins the covering axis to the screen and the scrollbar stays hidden. Ctrl+scroll zooms.
